  "q4_interpretation": "A LOCAL optimality check, not a distance from the global optimum. Each cell varies at most N route-periods across three ladder rungs centred on the delivered plan, so it establishes local optimality within that neighbourhood under the production objective, exactly. A plan can be optimal in every neighbourhood sampled here and still sit far from the best plan reachable by moving many route-periods at once. Use the figure as a LOWER bound on the differential-error bound: the full-problem differential can only be larger. A census margin below it is not distinguishable from treatment-correlated solver error; a margin above it is not thereby established, only not excluded by this measurement.",
